<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Balian of Ibelin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1143–1193</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Balian of Ibelin was a leading baron of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem</a> and the youngest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barisan-of-ibelin">Barisan of Ibelin</a>. In 1177 he married the dowager queen Maria Komnene, gaining <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nablus">Nablus</a>. After the defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hattin">Hattin</a> he led the defence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a> in 1187 and negotiated its surrender, allowing many inhabitants to ransom themselves. He later helped negotiate the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-jaffa-1192">Treaty of Jaffa</a> of 1192.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/balian-of-ibelin.jpg" alt="Balian of Ibelin" width="320" height="154" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Archer, Thomas Andrew; Kingsford, Charles Lethbridge · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sceau_de_Balian_d%27Ibelin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
